# Audit trail append-only (rule 248)

Owner design lock 2026-11-20 (evidence needs of A-02, A-05, A-30). Findings: AUD-01, AUD-02, AUD-03, AUD-04.

## Current state (verified 2026-11-20)

`sys_audit_logs` (every `RmeFinancialAuditEvent`) has no model guard and no trigger; its migration only describes it as
immutable. Financial event tables are immutable at the model layer only. `trx_lab_order_status_logs` cascades on
lab-order delete. This is implementation drift against this rule until it is implemented.

## Locked target

1. Layer 1 (independent of rule 245): model guards refuse update and delete; triggers refuse UPDATE, DELETE and TRUNCATE
   on `sys_audit_logs`, every financial and approval `*_events` table and `trx_lab_order_status_logs`; their foreign
   keys restrict on delete.
2. Layer 2 (with rule 245): the runtime holds SELECT and INSERT only on those tables.
3. Layer 3 (optional, detective): a hash chain verified read-only.
4. Patient merge records the moved ids in an append-only audit row, not only in a mutable case column.
5. An audit written after a rollback asserts transaction level 0.

No agent or operator prunes, edits or truncates these tables; retention is an owner decision executed by the owner role.

## Acceptance criteria

- On PostgreSQL 16, UPDATE, DELETE and TRUNCATE on each listed table fail (trigger now; also SQLSTATE 42501 after
  rule 245).
- Deleting a lab order that has status logs is refused; model update and delete throw; a merge writes one audit row
  listing the moved ids.
